# 3rok design system

> This is a substitute rule file. The original,
> `3rok-design-system/.cursor/rules/3rok-design-system.mdc`, was not in the
> repository, so this one was written from `3rok-design-system/` itself
> (`README.md`, `tokens.css`, `components/bundle.css`, `components/bundle.js`,
> `components/index.d.ts`) and the UI section of `docs/mvp-phase-plan.md`.
> If the original turns up, replace this file with a copy of it. Never edit
> anything inside `3rok-design-system/`.

## Setup

- Import once, in `app/layout.tsx` only:
  `import "../3rok-design-system/tokens.css";` then
  `import "../3rok-design-system/components/bundle.css";`
- The app is dark. `<html data-theme="dark">`. The light theme
  (`data-theme="light"`) is only for exported, printable reports.
- Do not load `components/bundle.js` and do not use `window.Rok`. Re-implement
  a component you need as a local `.tsx` in `components/ui/` that reuses the
  `rok-*` classes from `bundle.css`. `components/index.d.ts` documents the props.

## Color

- Use CSS variables only: `--surface-100/200/300`, `--ink`, `--ink-muted`,
  `--ink-subtle`, `--line`, `--line-strong`, `--accent`, `--on-accent`,
  `--status-nominal/caution/critical`, `--thermal-1` to `--thermal-5`.
- No hex, `rgb()` or `hsl()` in app code. `tests/design-gates.test.ts` fails on them.
- Status is shape plus word, never color alone (see `StatusBadge`: circle, triangle, square).
- Thermal ramp (`--thermal-*`) is for the placement map only.

## Type

- Barlow for words. IBM Plex Mono for every measured value.
- Display, heading, eyebrow and button styles are set in capitals by the CSS.
  Do not type them in capitals by hand, except the wordmark `3ROK`.
- Classes: `display-xl|lg|md`, `heading-lg|md|sm`, `body-lg|body|body-sm`,
  `eyebrow`, `button`, and the measured-value sizes `data-xl`, `data-md`,
  `data-sm`.
- Write the product name `3rok` in prose and `3ROK` in display type.

## Space and shape

- Spacing: `--space-1` to `--space-10` (4 px to 128 px). No other pixel gaps.
- Corners are square (`--radius-none`). `--radius-sm` (2 px) only on fields and badges.
- Borders are 1 px `--line`; stronger edges use `--line-strong`.
- Focus is the 2 px `--focus-ring` outline from `bundle.css`. Do not remove it.

## Buttons

- One `solid` button per screen. Everything else is `ghost` or `quiet`.
- Disabled buttons use the `disabled` attribute so `bundle.css` styles them.
- Per screen, the solid button is: `/account` `Sign in` (the create form uses
  `Create account`), `/cases` `Create case`, `/cases/[id]` `Ask Grok`,
  `/test` `Import case` until a file is loaded, then `Play path`.

## Components

Allowed: Button, NavBar, Panel, Stat, StatusBadge, Field, Tabs, DataTable.

- Not `Hero`. The home screen is not a marketing page.
- Not `ProgressBar` as a loss curve or as the Score region.
- `PlacementMap` only for record 7, the chip's place in the vehicle. Cell color
  there is that record's thermal coupling, with its `value_status` on the cell.
- Do not copy the design-system example labels `Run prediction`, `YR` or `KRAD`.
  Show lifetime or dose only when a record or `evaluate` returned it, with the
  unit from that source and the word `estimated` or the record's `value_status`.

## Words the UI must not use

- `project` for the saved container. It is a **case**.
- A training run, loss curve, checkpoint, epoch or fine-tune job. Grok reads the
  case. Its weights do not change.
